Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: HTMLparser.c
Line: 2726
Function: htmlParseData
Bug type: out-of-bounds-read
CWE: CWE-125
Explanation: When handling a carriage return, the code reads in[1] without checking that at least two bytes are available (avail >= 2). If the input buffer ends with a single '\r' (avail == 1), this dereferences one byte past the end of the buffer, causing an out-of-bounds read.

